	"_comment": "The grass decorations for the tests (flowers, plumes, spikes, corals), planted among their host grass types; DecoKinds loads it. Per kind: name; host = the grass type (a types.json name) it grows among; mode grid (spacing m; density = the share of cells planted) or clump (per_clump plumes per host clump; density); radius m (its reach), d_full m (full density out to), k_edge (the density kept at the reach), d_switch m (HIGH -> LOW mesh), fade_frac (the edge fade, a share of the radius); scale [min, max] (x the host's height when height_rel); bloom [[month, day] x4] = bud, bloom, bloom end, gone (wrapping the year), or \"always\"; palette entries [bud, bloom, seed] sRGB, or {\"flower\": c} (bud 60% toward leaf, seed 60% toward dry) or {\"colony\": c} (the same all year); cell [x, z] m the palette's patch; stem, centre sRGB; casts (shadows); cap [HIGH, LOW] instances; backlight; flutter; wind_response; hinge_response (1 = rotor wash and trails lay it over about its root, 0 = rigid); handoff_vis (the share of its coverage that shows over the host blades, for the colour handoff; 1.0 unless measured); patch_m, patch_share (it grows in patches); invented (made up for the game); mesh {builder, args} (DecoKinds._build_mesh). Heights are real-world sizes. Stems collapse in LOW, and the plumes and spider lilies cast no shadows (their HIGH shadow pass is costly). At most 32 kinds (DecoKinds.MAX_KINDS).",
